{
 "_doc": "Game event → sound (docs/10 §10.4; 02 §19.2 buses). js/audio/sfx-bridge.js turns each bus event into a key (e.g. `cast.ember`, `impact.rime`, `status.apply.soaked`, `fragment.land.large`, `pickup.oil`) and plays `events[key]` from the shared sfx catalog (sfx/data/catalog.json). `local` are recipes Lanternfall registers itself at load (Tide's spell.water.*: the shared catalog only holds elements avatar-3d/js/spellfx.js draws, and its node test enforces that), in the catalog's own entry format. `fallbacks` cover ids that have no recipe anywhere yet (05 §26's lf.* ids) or that a method cannot build; a missing id never goes silent. `pitch` / `gain` nudge a key (a jump is a softer, higher step). `fragments` = mass thresholds for the three crash sizes; `splashBig` = the fall speed (cells/s) that makes a splash big; `hardLand` = the fall (cells) that makes a landing loud. `pan` = cells from the camera centre at which a sound is hard left/right (01 §12.6 uses 240). Sounds the shared catalog gained for this game on 2026-09-26 (add-only): ambience.rain.light/heavy, rain.tick.metal, water.splash.small/big, water.pour, water.drain, steam.hiss, fire.whoosh, fire.crackle, ice.form, ice.crack, stone.crumble, fragment.crash.small/medium/large, lever.pull, door.grind, sluice.open, rope.creak, grapple.fire, lamp.relight, lamp.post, lantern.out, bell.toll, gutter.burst, rekindle, oil.pickup, pearl.pickup.",
